@api = http://localhost:5200
@keycloak = http://127.0.0.1:8180/realms/simple-demo

### 1. Log in as admin (password = username). Run this first; it stores the token for the requests below.
#    Swap username/password to "user" to test the other user.
POST {{keycloak}}/protocol/openid-connect/token
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

grant_type=password&client_id=simple-api&username=admin&password=admin

> {%
    client.global.set("token", response.body.access_token);
%}

### 2. Public, no token needed -> 200
GET {{api}}/public

### 3. Who am I? (any signed-in user) -> 200, shows name and roles
GET {{api}}/me
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 4. Needs role "user" -> 200 for admin and user
GET {{api}}/user
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 5. Needs role "admin" -> 200 for admin, 403 for user
GET {{api}}/admin
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 6. Without a token -> 401
GET {{api}}/admin
